  "review_notes": [
    "*made way for her* divides with *made* on the verb and *way* on יָדַיִם: the ASV spends an English word on each morpheme, so rule 2 splits the idiom rather than fusing it under rule 30.",
    "*the horse gate* renders the rectum attributively (rule 28); the one *the* stands before the rectum's own word and goes to the article on הַסּוּסִים, while the outer construct takes the supplied *the* of a multi-level chain."
